# Task Bootstrap

For any substantial user request, create or update a task directory under `tasks/` before substantive work begins.

Substantial includes:

- more than one meaningful step
- research, implementation, verification, or documentation work
- file, script, config, service, or durable artifact changes
- live checks against APIs, browsers, SSH, external systems, or runtime services
- work in another repository or absolute path outside this workspace
- follow-up work that continues the same non-trivial goal

Skip task creation only when the user explicitly opts out of task artifacts or the request is clearly trivial.

Use:

```bash
skills/task-creator/scripts/create_task.sh "Task title" "Short task description"
```

Chat does not replace `task.md`, `plan.md`, `findings.md`, or `verification.md`.
